# Login shells, interactive or not (an IDE or desktop session reading the
# environment), get mise's shims so its tools resolve without `mise activate`.
# Interactive shells activate mise on top in .zshrc (omz mise plugin), which
# puts the real tool dirs ahead of the shims. A static path, so login spawns no
# mise process; runs after macOS's /etc/zprofile path_helper, so it stays first.
typeset -U path PATH
path=("${MISE_DATA_DIR:-${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/mise}/shims" ~/.local/bin $path)
